# FunHub Software Architecture Document

## Purpose

This document describes the technical architecture of the FunHub platform.

The goal is to create a secure, scalable, and reliable entertainment platform capable of serving customers and businesses across Nigeria and eventually Africa.

---

# System Overview

FunHub consists of four major applications:

## 1. Customer Mobile Application

Technology:

Flutter

Purpose:

Allows customers to:

- Discover entertainment locations.
- Search nearby experiences.
- View offers.
- Make reservations.
- Make payments.
- Share experiences.

---

## 2. Business Platform

Technology:

Flutter

Purpose:

Allows businesses to:

- Register their company.
- Manage locations.
- Create offers.
- Respond to customers.
- Manage bookings.
- View business analytics.

---

## 3. Admin Dashboard

Technology:

React + TypeScript

Purpose:

Allows FunHub administrators to:

- Verify businesses.
- Manage users.
- Monitor transactions.
- Manage reports.

---

## 4. Backend API

Technology:

NestJS + TypeScript

Purpose:

The backend controls:

- Authentication.
- User management.
- Business management.
- Bookings.
- Payments.
- Reviews.
- Notifications.

---

# Database

Technology:

PostgreSQL

Purpose:

Stores:

- Users.
- Businesses.
- Locations.
- Bookings.
- Payments.
- Reviews.
- Transactions.

---

# Database Management

Technology:

Prisma ORM

Purpose:

Provides:

- Database models.
- Secure database queries.
- Type safety.
- Migration management.

---

# Infrastructure

Technology:

Docker

Purpose:

Ensures every environment runs consistently.

Docker will manage:

- Backend services.
- Database services.
- Development environment.

---

# System Communication

The communication flow:

Customer App

↓

Backend API

↓

Database


Business App

↓

Backend API

↓

Database


Admin Dashboard

↓

Backend API

↓

Database

---

# Security Principles

FunHub will implement:

- Encrypted communication.
- Secure password storage.
- Role-based permissions.
- Authentication tokens.
- Audit logging.
- Data protection practices.

---

# Scalability Plan

The architecture should support growth from:

100 users

to

Millions of users.

The system will be designed with:

- Modular services.
- Database optimization.
- Cloud deployment.
- Performance monitoring.

---

# Future Expansion

The architecture should allow integration with:

- Hotels.
- Flights.
- Transportation services.
- Payment providers.
- AI recommendation systems.
- Tourism services.

---

# Engineering Principle

Build simple first.

Scale when needed.

Every technical decision must support FunHub's mission of making entertainment planning effortless.
